{
  "name": "Afro-Synonyms",
  "version": "afro-1.3",
  "createdAt": "2026-07-26",
  "purpose": "Concept-level equivalences, expanded into the query before retrieval. The manifest names tools in institutional register — 'childbirth budget', 'crop rotation planner', 'loan comparison', 'currency converter' — while people ask in everyday words: 'deliver baby', 'what to plant after maize', 'borrow', 'change pounds to cedis'. Neither the phrase lexicon nor per-tool synonyms close that, because the gap is one word standing for another across the whole catalogue.",
  "method": "Expansion, not replacement: the original token is always kept and its synonyms appended, so a synonym can only add reach and never removes a match the retriever would otherwise have made.",
  "discipline": "Written as general language facts, deliberately covering far more concepts than any benchmark exercises. Groups are bidirectional — every term in a group expands to every other.",
